# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts.
# Deliberately NOT `coverage.*`: that pattern also swallows source files such as
# a coverage.go, which then never shows up in `git status` (the same silent-loss
# class as the tracked-and-ignored directory this file used to carry).
*.out
coverage.html
coverage.txt
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# External test fixtures (downloaded, not committed)
**/testdata/external/

# Common Crawl test corpus (fetched via `make fetch-cc`, never committed)
testdata/corpus/

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# The batched harvest's failure catalogs (testdata/cc/batch-quarantine.tsv and
# testdata/cc/stress/batch-quarantine.tsv) are deliberately NOT ignored: they
# are references only (digest, crawl, query-stripped url, stage, signature),
# they are the durable record of a 30k+-reference harvest that costs days of
# fetching and loses files to link rot on every re-run, and they sit next to
# known_failures.tsv, which has always been committed. See testdata/cc/HARVEST.md.
# The ledger and attempts sidecar stay ignored — they live under
# testdata/corpus/ and are pure machine-local progress state.
